From 73cc01d1ea99dac69c388665cc92b3a081561ecd Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Wed, 23 Sep 2026 08:03:42 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 3/5] Record the new speed and applying rules in receipts, and
 keep reading old ones

A receipt states its conventions, and validation accepted exactly one set.
Once the speeds and the applying rule changed, the true set could no longer
be the one rc.3 to rc.6 recorded. A single fixed set would then have made
every receipt from those versions unreadable: downloaded receipts, saved
records and the compare tool.

The rc.3 to rc.6 set is frozen as CONVENTIONS_RC3. The current set differs
in two tokens:

- speed: "central-difference-plus-minus-0.001-day;nodes-plus-minus-0.25-day"
- aspects: adds "applying-instantaneous-orb-rate"

A receipt must match one set exactly; a mixed set is unsupported_feature.
The old set is accepted only from engine versions 0.1.1-rc.3 to rc.6. For
the current set, every aspect's applying flag must agree with aspectMotion
on the recorded longitudes and speeds, or the receipt is
inconsistent_result. Old receipts are never judged by the new rule.
NATAL_RECEIPT_CONVENTION_SETS lists both sets.

src/fixtures/receipt-rc6.json was serialized by the published rc.6 package
nine minutes before the new moon of 2027-01-07. It records the Sun-Moon
conjunction as not applying, which is the defect. The tests check four
things. It still parses and replays, and it stays accepted with that flag
flipped. The current receipt marks the conjunction applying and is refused
with it flipped. A mixed set, a foreign set and an rc.6 receipt relabelled
rc.7 are refused. The fixture is kept byte-identical, out of Prettier's
reach.

